{
  "title": "Pustulosis Palmoplantaris",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/4037/pustulosis-palmoplantaris",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 18 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pustulosis Palmoplantaris, also known as pustular psoriasis, is an idiopathic skin condition commonly seen in smokers, that presents with crops of sterile pustules that occur on one or both hands and feet.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is one of exclusion and is made with the presence of 1 to 10 mm sterile pustules on palms or feet with surrounding erythema and fissures. No serological tests are specific for disease.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually general measures such as smoking cessation, avoiding skin irritants, and medical management with topical corticosteroids.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "more common in middle-aged **men** than in women",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "rare in children",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the majority of patients are **smokers** (65–90%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "increased stress",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "infection (i.e acute or chronic tonsillitis)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "drugs (i.e.TNF-alpha inhibitors)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "unknown",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "therories",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "activated **nicotine receptors** in the sweat glands cause an **inflammatory process**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
